    "unresolved": [
      "The file note carries no year: it is dated 'Tues, wk of 1 June'. The year 2026 comes only from the decision log, a later restatement of the note; the month is common to both. If the year is 2026 the note's date denotes Tuesday 2 June 2026; the date is carried as 2026-06 and not completed.",
      "Whether the day the note was written is the day the extension was agreed is not stated.",
      "The agreement is verbal. The letter Calder was to send 'by end of month' is not in the material, so a written agreement, its date and its terms are not evidenced; that the extension took effect rests on later material only.",
      "The owner rests on the note's heading, 'P. Nandakumar', read with its first-person 'Within my limit'. The post (Finance Director) is supplied only by the OIC minute of 9 April and the decision log.",
      "The limit the note states names no instrument, so no authority is contributed. That the Scheme of Delegation's paragraph 4.4 has terms covering the act is reported as an applicability finding beside this candidate.",
      "Every context contribution drawn from the file note grades indeterminate for contemporaneity: the note carries no time that has a basis (no year), and consideration does not lift a time-less artefact. They are held as evidence and are not presented as contemporaneous context.",
      "The budget source was to be checked ('Check with Karen'); no confirmation is in the material.",
      "Whether data export tools stay licensed during the extension is not evidenced.",
      "The decision log, as at 30 September 2026, shows the report of the extension to the OIC as open (A-26-045, due 11 June) and the file note as 'not yet seen by OIC'.",
      "The decision log's 'File note' is not otherwise identified; that it is this note rests on the matching subject, period and post-holder.",
      "No statement of what reversing the extension would cost is in the material; the proportionality tier is undetermined."
    ],
